has two white streaks in otherwise dark hair, a broad nose and a deep dimple on one cheek, and a favorite piece of clothing, a narrow-striped sweater. It usually goes with a narrow brass watch set a little fast. When somebody else has the floor, Keiko starts to lift a hand, then waits to be invited to speak.","personality":"Keiko never tires of being shown how somebody makes a living. Keiko can ask an expert question of a craftsperson and still mishandle a simple emotional cue from a friend.","agenda":"To leave a warm bun on a lonely doorstep.","family":"Grey Good is Keiko’s half-sibling. Keiko chooses whether they walk home or sit a while. Grey brings a spare shopping bag. That small arrangement gives both a reason to see each other on weeks when asking for company outright feels difficult. Asked about *A wall of birthdays*, Grey says, “I papered over the wall because my boy never reached his next mark.”","connections":"Layla Jimenez. A cook who can't smell can still follow a holiday gift to the right neighbor.","familyIds":["AH-R0232"],"connectionIds":["AH-R0694"],"reactions":[{"situation":"A customer wants a bun saved until evening","response":"Keiko writes the customer's name and collection time on the wrapped bun.","asWritten":"A customer wants a bun saved until evening. Keiko writes the customer's name and collection time on the wrapped bun."},{"situation":"A coworker arrives late after a night at the hospital","response":"Keiko asks them privately what can be shared about the delay and respects the answer.","asWritten":"A coworker arrives late after a night at the hospital. Keiko asks them privately what can be shared about the delay and respects the answer."},{"situation":"When a relative hints at needing company","response":"Keiko may initially offer a repair, but sits down as soon as the request becomes clear.","asWritten":"When a relative hints at needing company, Keiko may initially offer a repair, but sits down as soon as the request becomes clear."}]},